<title>USA: Liggett packs to have new warnings - WSJ.</title>
<headline>Liggett packs to have new warnings - WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>New warning labels are about to grace packs of cigarettes on brands produced by Liggett Group, the result of a landmark settlement by the tobacco company, the Wall Street Journal said.</p>
<p>In Thursday's electronic edition, the Journal said the label will read in small print: &quot;Warning: Smoking is addictive.&quot;</p>
<p>The warning is to appear on Liggett brands, including Eve, L&amp;M and Chesterfield. Liggett is a unit of Brooke Group Ltd .</p>
<p>The new label is expected to show up on packs that arrive in stores in the next week.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
